collision is a property of a published coding scheme rather than something
constructed to demonstrate one.

The annotators worked six levels and the three-level \code{label} is their
collapse. Both mixed levels fold to their own polarity, so \code{Neutral} means no
sentiment content and nothing else. Ambiguity lives in \code{M_Positive} and
\code{M_Negative}, which are inside the positive and negative classes rather than
